    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "# 🔧 Technologies Used in Real-Time Bitcoin Anomaly Detection Project"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "This notebook introduces and summarizes the core technologies used in the Bitcoin Anomaly Detection pipeline. It includes setup, usage examples, and integration details for each component."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## Amazon Kinesis\n",
                "**Kinesis Data Streams** is used for ingesting real-time Bitcoin data. It can scale horizontally to handle high-throughput event ingestion.\n",
                "\n",
                "### Key CLI Commands:"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {},
            "execution_count": None,
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "!aws kinesis create-stream --stream-name bitcoin-price-stream --shard-count 1\n",
                "!aws kinesis delete-stream --stream-name bitcoin-price-stream"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Python Integration:"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {},
            "execution_count": None,
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "import boto3, json\n",
                "client = boto3.client('kinesis')\n",
                "client.put_record(StreamName='bitcoin-price-stream', Data=json.dumps({\"price\": 31000}), PartitionKey='pk')"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## AWS Lambda\n",
                "**Lambda** is used to apply ML model logic (anomaly detection) in a serverless way.\n",
                "\n",
                "### Packaging and Deployment:"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {},
            "execution_count": None,
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Inside Docker:\n",
                "pip install numpy==1.19.5 scikit-learn==0.24.2 joblib -t python/\n",
                "cp handler.py python/ && cd python && zip -r9 ../lambda.zip ."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Permissions:\n",
                "- `kinesis:GetRecords`, `kinesis:DescribeStream`, etc.\n",
                "- `sns:Publish` for alerts\n",
                "- `firehose:PutRecord` to archive anomalies\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## Kinesis Firehose\n",
                "Used to archive both raw and processed data to **Amazon S3** for later analysis and visualization."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {},
            "execution_count": None,
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Example Firehose config (in JSON file):\n",
                "{\n",
                "  \"RoleARN\": \"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/firehose_delivery_role\",\n",
                "  \"BucketARN\": \"arn:aws:s3:::btc-anomaly-data\"\n",
                "}\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## Amazon QuickSight\n",
                "Used for interactive dashboarding of Bitcoin trends and anomalies.\n",
                "\n",
                "**Steps to Use:**\n",
                "1. Create Athena table over S3-partitioned data\n",
                "2. Grant access to QuickSight via IAM\n",
                "3. Import data source → visualize\n",
                "\n",
                "**Supports filters, color-coding, dual-axis charts.**"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## Apache Flink\n",
                "**Apache Flink on Kinesis (Managed Service)** was used to compute rolling average and detect spikes.\n",
                "\n",
                "- Job packaged as **JAR** using Maven:\n",
                "```bash\n",
                "mvn clean package\n",
                "```\n",
                "- Uploaded to S3\n",
                "- Referenced in Flink console during application creation\n"
            ]
        }
    ],
